  {
   "id": 511226,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<span data-math=\"x + {y^2} = 1\">x + {y^2} = 1</span>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"x + {y^2} = 1\"></span></td>\n<td>Isolate the <i>y</i> term.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"x + {y^2} - x = 1 - x\"></span></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"{y^2} = 1 - x\"></span></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"y = \\pm \\sqrt {1 - x} \"></span></td>\n<td>Use the Square Root Property.</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Substitute 0 for <i>x</i>.</p>\n<p><i>y</i> = 1 and –1.</p>\n<p>Thus, you have two <i>y</i>-values paired with one <i>x</i>-value. This is not a function.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "not a function"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 511227,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<span data-math=\"y-{x^2} = 2\">y-{x^2} = 2</span>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"y - {x^2} = 2\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"y = {x^2} + 2\"></span></p>\n<p>You square <i>x</i>, then add 2. Since each value of <i>x</i> will correspond to just one value of <i>y</i>, this is a function.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "function"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
